---
description: Never add AI tool attribution to commits, commit messages, code or docs
alwaysApply: true
---

Strict rule from the repository owner. It applies to every task in this workspace
and to all nested repositories (Pasado, neptune, Local-Lipschitz-Constants).

- Never write or allow any AI attribution in a commit message: no
  `Co-authored-by` or `Co-Authored-By` trailers naming an AI tool, no
  "Generated with", no AI tool names or tool email addresses.
- Do not run `git commit` or `git commit --amend` from the agent environment,
  because that environment can append such a trailer on its own. Prepare the
  changes and give the owner the exact commands to run in their own terminal.
  If a commit is absolutely necessary, write it with plumbing
  (`git commit-tree` plus `git update-ref`) using a message that contains only
  what the owner approved, then read the stored message back and confirm it
  has no attribution line.
- Code comments, docstrings, docs and logs must not mention AI tools either.
- Before any push, scan the commits to be pushed for attribution lines and stop
  if one is found.
- Commits use the owner's identity: Dimitrije Pešić <dimitrije.pesicc@gmail.com>.
  Never change the global git identity.
